A project that sets `--boogie` arguments can now load the standard libraries and other libraries (`.doo` files).  Before, the project's `--boogie` arguments had to equal the library's exactly.  Now only the arguments that could change which facts an imported declaration contributes have to match.  The arguments that may differ are on an explicit, reviewed list: at present `/normalizeDeclarationOrder`, `/structuralLiterals`, `/cacheBackground` and `/scheduleByImplementation`, in their bare form or with the value 0 or 1.  Any other argument, and any argument not on the list, is still checked, so a mismatch gives the same error as before.  The hidden option `--legacy-boogie-library-check` restores the exact comparison.
